<article class="env-corollary" id="031V">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/031V">Corollary <span data-tag="031V">7.3.9.4</span>.</a> Let $U: \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}$ be a cocartesian fibration of $\infty $-categories, let $K$ be a weakly contractible simplicial set, and let $\overline{f}: K^{\triangleright } \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ be a diagram. The following conditions are equivalent: </p>
<p><dl>
<dt>$(1)$</dt>
<dd><p>
The diagram $\overline{f}$ carries each edge of $K^{\triangleright }$ to a $U$-cocartesian morphism of $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$. 
</p>
</dd>
<dt>$(2)$</dt>
<dd><p>
The restriction $f = \overline{f}|_{K}$ carries each edge of $K$ to a $U$-cocartesian morphism of $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}$, and $\overline{f}$ is a $U$-colimit diagram. 
</p>
</dd>
</dl></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      Without loss of generality, we may assume that $f$ carries each edge of $K$ to a $U$-cocartesian morphism of $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$. Let $\pi : \Delta ^1 \times K^{\triangleright } \rightarrow K^{\triangleright }$ be the morphism which is the identity on $\{ 0\}  \times K^{\triangleright }$ and which carries $\{ 1\}  \times K^{\triangleright }$ to the cone point $v \in K^{\triangleright }$. Set $D = f(v) \in \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ and $E = U(D) \in \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}$. Proposition <a data-tag="01VK" href="/tag/01VK">5.2.1.3</a> guarantees that the lifting problem 
    <p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ \{ 0\}  \times K^{\triangleright } \ar [r]^-{ \overline{f}} \ar [d] &amp;  \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}\ar [d]^{U} \\ \Delta ^1 \times K^{\triangleright } \ar [r]^-{U \circ \overline{f} \circ \pi } \ar@ {--&gt;}[ur]^{ \alpha } &amp;  \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}} \]
</div>
<p>
       admits a solution $\alpha : \Delta ^1 \times K^{\triangleright } \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ which carries $\Delta ^1 \times \{ x\} $ to a $U$-cocartesian morphism of $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$, for each vertex $x \in K^{\triangleright }$. Set $\overline{g} = \alpha |_{ \{ 1\}  \times K^{\triangleright }}$, which we regard as a morphism from $K^{\triangleright }$ to the $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}_{E}$, and let us identify $\alpha $ with a natural transformation from $\overline{f}$ to $\overline{g}$. Note that $\alpha _{v}: \overline{f}(v) \rightarrow \overline{g}(v)$ is a $U$-cocartesian morphism of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ satisfying $U(\alpha _ v) = \operatorname{id}_{E}$, and is therefore an isomorphism (Proposition <a data-tag="01TB" href="/tag/01TB">5.1.1.9</a>). Applying Proposition <a data-tag="031R" href="/tag/031R">7.3.9.3</a>, we can reformulate $(2)$ as follows: 
    <p>
<dl>
<dt>$(2')$</dt>
<dd><p>
The morphism $\overline{g}: K^{\triangleright } \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}_{E}$ is a $U$-colimit diagram in $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$. 
</p>
</dd>
</dl>
<p>
      Set $g = \overline{g}|_{K}$. For every edge $u: x \rightarrow y$ of $K$, we have a commutative diagram 
    <p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ f(x) \ar [r]^-{ f(u) } \ar [d]^{ \alpha _ x} &amp;  f(y) \ar [d]^{ \alpha _ y} \\ g(x) \ar [r]^-{ g(u) } &amp;  g(y) } \]
</div>
<p>
       in the $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ where the morphisms $f(u)$, $\alpha _ x$, and $\alpha _ y$ are $U$-cocartesian. Applying Corollary <a data-tag="01TS" href="/tag/01TS">5.1.2.4</a>, we deduce that $g(u)$ is $U$-cocartesian when viewed as a morphism of $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$, and is therefore an isomorphism in the $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}_{E}$ (Proposition <a data-tag="01TB" href="/tag/01TB">5.1.1.9</a>). Similarly, for every vertex $x \in K$, the unique edge $c_{x}: x \rightarrow v$ of $K^{\triangleright }$ determines a commutative diagram 
    <p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ f(x) \ar [r]^-{\overline{f}(c_ x)} \ar [d]^{ \alpha _ x} &amp;  \overline{f}(v) \ar [d]^{ \alpha _ v} \\ g(x) \ar [r]^-{ \overline{g}(c_ x)} &amp;  \overline{g}(v), } \]
</div>
<p>
       where $\alpha _{x}$ is $U$-cocartesian and $\alpha _{v}$ is an isomorphism. Combining Corollary <a data-tag="01TS" href="/tag/01TS">5.1.2.4</a>, Corollary <a data-tag="01TT" href="/tag/01TT">5.1.2.5</a>, and Proposition <a data-tag="01TB" href="/tag/01TB">5.1.1.9</a>, we see that $\overline{f}(c_ x)$ is $U$-cocartesian if and only if $\overline{g}(c_ x)$ is an isomorphism in the $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}_{E}$. We can therefore reformulate condition $(1)$ as follows: 
    <p>
<dl>
<dt>$(1')$</dt>
<dd><p>
The diagram $\overline{g}$ carries each edge of $K^{\triangleright }$ to an isomorphism in the $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}_{E}$. 
</p>
</dd>
</dl>
<p>
       By virtue of Corollary <a data-tag="02XX" href="/tag/02XX">7.2.3.5</a>, $(1')$ is equivalent to the requirement that $\overline{g}$ is a colimit diagram in the $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}_{E}$. In particular, the implication $(2') \Rightarrow (1')$ follows from Corollary <a data-tag="02KY" href="/tag/02KY">7.1.7.8</a>. To prove the converse, it will suffice to show that condition $(1')$ is satisfied, then for every morphism $u: E \rightarrow E'$ in $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}$, the covariant transport functor $u_{!}: \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}_{E} \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}_{E'}$ carries $\overline{g}$ to a colimit diagram in the $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}_{E'}$ (Corollary <a data-tag="06A0" href="/tag/06A0">7.1.7.16</a>). This follows immediately from Corollary <a data-tag="02XX" href="/tag/02XX">7.2.3.5</a> (applied to the composite diagram $K^{\triangleleft } \xrightarrow { \overline{g} } \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}_{E} \xrightarrow { u_{!} } \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}_{E'}$). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</p></p></p></p></p></p></p></p></p></p></article>
